@prefix agp: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov#> .
@prefix bl: <https://dagalog.no/ns/backlog#> .
@prefix ghissues: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/issues/> .
@prefix ghpull: <https://github.com/daghovland/rdf-datalog/pull/> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix session: <https://dagalog.no/ns/agentprov/session#> .

# PROSPECTIVE summary scaffold, generated by scripts/new-provenance-summary.sh.
# TODO: replace the placeholder summaryText/decisionPoint below with the
# actual distilled reasoning behind this PR before committing — see
# docs/plans/TRANSCRIPT_SUMMARY_GUIDELINES.md. Timestamps below are real
# (from `git log main..HEAD` on branch fix/546-rml-flaky-test); everything else that
# isn't marked TODO can be left as-is.

ghpull:555 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "rml: incorporate a UUID into write_temp's tempdir path across tests/, fixing the concurrent-worktree race" ;
    bl:number 555 ;
    bl:state bl:Open ;
    bl:closesIssue ghissues:546 .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr555 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:546 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-08-13T22:23:27+02:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-08-18T18:05:16Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr555Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #546 was itself discovered as a side effect of running the quality gate for the unrelated #495 (RmlError thiserror conversion): rml/tests/xml_source_tests.rs's write_temp helper built a fixed tempdir path from only the caller-supplied file name, so concurrent cargo test --workspace runs across different git worktrees (this repo's normal multi-agent workflow) could race on the same path and produce intermittent assertion failures. #229 had already fixed the identical bug class in rml/tests/security_tests.rs's temp_dir helper by incorporating uuid::Uuid::new_v4() into the directory name, so that was the direct precedent applied here rather than inventing a new approach. The issue explicitly suggested auditing rml/tests/ for other instances of the same pattern; doing so found two more -- csv_tests.rs's write_temp_csv and json_tests.rs's write_temp -- both fixed identically. Verification leaned on cargo test -p rml directly (all three affected files plus the rest of the crate, including the originally-flaking xml_source_nested_iterator test) since the race is inherently about concurrent worktree execution and isolated single-process runs wouldn't prove much either way; the fix is also structurally obviously correct (a UUID-suffixed path makes collision impossible by construction), so a full concurrent-reproduction harness wasn't built. A secondary orchestration note: the implementing sub-agent stalled repeatedly waiting on its own backgrounded cargo commands, and separately, this session's shared CARGO_TARGET_DIR filled to 100% disk usage mid-task (triggering two independent cargo clean calls from different agents working in parallel worktrees, which collided and forced some rebuilds) -- neither affected the correctness of the final fix, but did extend how long verification took." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:555 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr555 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .

